---
description: Git Commit Message Guidelines
alwaysApply: false
priority: highest
---

### headers  
Message must start with following headers  

- **[Release]**: Major feature (e.g. project completion); use for the final commit when pushing to the main server. 
- **[Developing]**: Work in progress. Use when a Feat is not yet complete. Commits for temporary code storage. 
- **[Feat]**: Feature   
- **[Chore]**: Routine maintenance tasks or trivial work that does not directly affect the functionality of the code.
- **[Refactor]**: Code refactoring (code cleanup).   
- **[UI]**: User interface. 
- **[Bugfix]**: Bug fix. Use for fixes made after a Feat.   
- **[Hotfix]**: Hotfix; for urgent changes when a detailed commit message is omitted. 
- **[Docs]**: Documentation (e.g. dev docs, comments).   
- **[I18n]**: Use for translation.  

### description  
after header and title, you should write description in Chinese with list format. description must be specific and detailed. 

### example  
[Bugfix] 修复审批流审批状态显示问题